{
  "biological_interpretation": "E1 and E2 loss in the UFMylation cascade share a selective posterior neuronal response with Ddit3 induction and V-ATPase repression, supporting a pathway-specific UFMylation-defect state rather than generic ER knockdown alone.",
  "caveats": [
    "Ufsp2 is less interchangeable with Uba5/Ufc1 than Uba5 and Ufc1 are with each other.",
    "Several responsive classes lack FDR-confirmed Ufc1 or Ufsp2 transcript depletion despite coherent downstream signatures."
  ],
  "cell_types": [
    "151 TH Prkcd Grin2c Glut",
