    "066 CNU-HYa HY GABA"
  ],
  "exact_observed_result": "Uba5 and Ufc1 perturbations converged strongly in 151 TH Prkcd Grin2c Glut and 155 MB Glut, inducing Ddit3/Eef1a1/Ndufa2-linked stress genes and repressing Atp6v0c and synaptic or RNA-processing transcripts. Ufsp2 produced a related but narrower response, clearest in 155 MB Glut.",
  "preliminary_scores": {
    "novelty": 3,
    "priority": 5,
    "support": 5
  },
  "prior_expectation": "UBA5 and UFC1 are the UFM1 E1 and E2 enzymes, and human UBA5/UFC1 defects cause severe neurodevelopmental disease; the observed Ddit3 and V-ATPase response is a plausible neuronal UFMylation-loss readout.",
